WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.860
The Marvel Cinematic Universe is a vast narrative
that grows more expansive and complex with

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.860
each movie.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:09.910
Directors Joe and Anthony Russo managed to
work a healthy chunk of that universe into

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.780
Avengers: Endgame, but there isn't always
room for everyone.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.780
As much as we may have wanted to see them,
here's why we didn't see these characters

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.120
in Endgame.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.880
Stellan Skarsgård’s Dr. Erik Selvig can't
boast any magical powers or high-tech suits

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.090
of armor, but he was integral early on the
MCU.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.840
Appearing in the first two Thor films as well
as the first two Avengers movies, we last

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.860
saw Selvig in 2015's Age of Ultron helping
Thor recapture his vision of the Infinity

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:34.860
Stones.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.440
A week before Endgame's premiere, Skarsgård
confirmed he wasn’t part of the cast.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.260
"I've done four [Marvel films] and they have
me contracted for five and they haven't called

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.260
me yet.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.550
They usually call me when they need some weird
plot to be explained in a quasi-scientific

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:47.550
way."

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:51.800
Selvig entered the MCU as part of Thor's entourage,
but that was before the game-changing Thor:

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.890
Ragnarok, which was the first entry of the
Thor franchise to not involve him, Natalie

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:57.360
Portman, or Kat Dennings.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.430
It was also unquestionably the most successful
in that franchise.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:05.320
Ragnarok's success made Skarsgård part of
a Thor paradigm that the MCU may not be interested

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.320
in anymore.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:11.000
As soon as it was revealed that Game of Thrones
star Peter Dinklage would appear in Avengers:

00:01:11.009 --> 00:01:14.400
infinity War, there was wild speculation about
who the actor would play.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.799
A brief exchange in a preview clip left fans
incorrectly believing that Dinklage was voicing

00:01:18.799 --> 00:01:20.999
Black Order member Corvus Glaive.

00:01:20.999 --> 00:01:25.590
Dinklage was instead revealed as Eitri the
Dwarf, the forgemaster of Nidavellir who made

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:28.310
Mjolnir and whom Thor seeks out for a new
weapon.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:32.819
He doesn't appear in Endgame, and we don't
even know if Eitri survives the decimation.

00:01:32.819 --> 00:01:36.380
Whether he does or not, he'd still be left
alone on Nidavellir since all his dwarven

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.120
brethren were killed before the snap even
happened.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:45.720
"Then he killed everyone anyway.

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:48.049
All except me."

00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:52.009
Presumably, with Stormbreaker made and the
first battle with Thanos fought and lost,

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:54.599
Eitri's work in the Infinity Saga was over.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.840
But it would be gratifying to find out how
the forgemaster is faring.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:02.239
When Steve Rogers and Tony Stark lose the
Tesseract to Loki and are forced to go back

00:02:02.239 --> 00:02:06.619
to 1970 to get their hands on the Space Stone,
we get to see some old friends.

00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:10.549
Tony is reunited with a young Howard Stark
and we even get a brief conversation between

00:02:10.549 --> 00:02:12.900
Howard and Edwin Jarvis from Agent Carter.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:17.290
Peggy Carter herself is accounted for as well
when Cap notices her through an office window.

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:22.530
And a digitally de-aged Michael Douglas appears
as Hank Pym when Rogers visits his lab.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:24.950
Conspicuously absent is Toby Jones’ Dr.
Arnim Zola.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:28.900
Viewers might not even have taken note of
the absence, but when Howard first runs into

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.780
Tony, he's looking for the Hydra veteran.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.760
Zola likely doesn't appear because it wouldn't
serve the plot of an already crowded film.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.980
There's also a convenient narrative explanation
for his absence.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.920
In Captain America: The Winter Soldier, the
Zola A.I. explains why he lives in a computer:

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:46.520
"In 1972, I received a terminal diagnosis.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.920
Science could not save my body."

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.719
Whatever that diagnosis was, it's possible
he was already suffering its effects in 1970,

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:58.280
which could go along way toward explaining
why he wasn't at work that day.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:03.560
To capture the Power Stone, Nebula and War
Machine travel to Morag in 2014, just as Peter

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.670
Quill was about to nab it in the beginning
of Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:10.709
Unlike that earlier film, Djimon Hounsou’s
Kree warrior Korath doesn't show up with his

00:03:10.709 --> 00:03:13.129
soldiers to attempt to get the Orb back from
Quill.

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:16.959
Narratively, the reason for Korath's absence
can be explained by an unfortunate development

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:18.040
for the Avengers.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:22.650
Sending Nebula back to 2014 has the unintended
consequence of alerting the Thanos of that

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.400
time what the Avengers are up to.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.319
Once Thanos' forces detect the signal from
the 2019 Nebula, they set course for Morag

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:29.700
and eventually capture her.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.660
So while Korath who works for Ronan, who is
working for Thanos is heading to Morag, Thanos

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.230
himself is en route, too.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:38.760
The Kree warrior wouldn't be dumb enough to
try to get in Thanos' way once he learns he

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:41.480
shares a destination with his boss's boss.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:46.469
The trio Hank Pym calls the "Wombats" in Ant-Man
skilled storyteller Luis, played by Michael

00:03:46.469 --> 00:03:50.969
Peña; Kurt, played by David Dastmalchian;
and Dave, played by T.I., don’t show up

00:03:50.969 --> 00:03:51.969
in the film.

00:03:51.969 --> 00:03:55.230
You could argue Luis at least is there in
spirit, as we hear his famous musical car

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:59.200
horn several times, but the group themselves
choose to, as they say, "back it up."

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:07.670
While Luis has proven he's got a punch you
do not want to be on the receiving end of,

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:11.690
neither Kurt nor Dave have shown us they'd
be very effective against alien soldiers or

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:16.030
other superpowered baddies, so the Wombats
would be little help against Thanos' forces.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:20.169
Still, an alternate version of Endgame that's
simply Luis' retelling of the events would

00:04:20.169 --> 00:04:21.360
be a great time.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.960
When Thor and Rocket go back to the events
of Thor: The Dark World to retrieve the Aether,

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:30.590
the thunder god has what proves to be a much-needed
reunion with his mother Frigga who, later

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.849
that day, is fated to lose her life.

00:04:32.849 --> 00:04:36.640
Though she appears in both of the first two
Thor films, Frigga might have wound up getting

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:40.830
more more lines and screen time in Endgame
than in the two earlier films combined.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:43.080
Thor doesn't get to see his father Odin, however.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:47.319
At this point in the MCU's timeline, Odin
is in denial about his son's place in Asgard

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:51.720
and the return of the Dark Elves, and soon
he'll be in denial about his chances against

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:52.720
the Dark Elves.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:56.340
When Frigga speaks with Thor, her husband
is likely meeting with his generals about

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:58.160
the invasion that won't happen.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:02.480
The absence of Jaimie Alexander’s Sif in
Avengers: Endgame, is an indicator we've seen

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.699
our last of the character in the MCU.

00:05:04.699 --> 00:05:09.120
Alexander is also conspicuously absent from
2017's Thor: Ragnarok.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:13.361
Marvel Studios President Kevin Feige explained
that Loki, disguised as Odin, wouldn't want

00:05:13.361 --> 00:05:17.640
Thor's closest allies to threaten his rule,
so when he accuses Heimdall of treason, he

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.490
also exiles Sif from Asgard.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:23.300
The real-world reason for her absence was
much simpler: scheduling.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:27.580
According to Alexander, Marvel waited until
the last minute to ask her to appear in Ragnarok,

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:31.750
at which point Marvel's shooting schedule
conflicted with that of Alexander’s NBC

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.349
series Blindspot.

00:05:33.349 --> 00:05:35.610
As of Endgame, Sif is still a no-show.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:39.160
She isn't with the refugees in New Asgard,
and she doesn't appear at the final battle

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:40.560
with the resurrected heroes.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.670
By the end of the film Thor is headed back
to the stars, so it's possible we might see

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:45.670
a reunion.

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:49.410
But as the years tick by it feels less and
less likely that one of the MCU's fiercest

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.280
warrior women will return.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:56.680
Phil Coulson, played by Clark Gregg, is killed
by Loki in 2012's Avengers, but like a true

00:05:56.680 --> 00:06:00.830
Marvel hero he's resurrected in time to star
in Marvel's Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:03.949
But if you didn't watch Marvel's TV shows,
you'd never know that.

00:06:03.949 --> 00:06:08.560
Considering how famously fractured the movie
and television sides of the MCU have been,

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:10.680
Coulson has been cinematically dead since
Avengers.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:15.139
Still, ever since his traumatic televised
revival, fans of the MCU have wondered whether

00:06:15.139 --> 00:06:17.711
Coulson would ever get the chance to let his
old friends know he was back.

00:06:17.711 --> 00:06:22.220
It sure seems like Endgame is just about the
last chance Coulson has to give the Avengers

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:23.230
an FYI.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:27.270
But Coulson's nowhere to be seen in Endgame,
and Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.'s fifth season

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.419
ends with Coulson learning he is dying.

00:06:29.419 --> 00:06:32.080
He chooses to retire to Tahiti with Melinda
May.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.320
To further complicate things, in season 6,
Coulson will be dead and Gregg will play a

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:37.480
new character.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:41.500
To include Coulson in Endgame, the filmmakers
would need to explain Coulson's confusing

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:46.170
status to film audiences, along with everything
else on their to-do list for Endgame.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:50.580
All parties probably agreed it was best for
him to stay on the TV side of things for now.

